<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Sumpgas.xml                       UtinniPatches — SUMP_GASLIGHT_1

  Item spec §1, the reaction: "tar + acid -> green gas (Helixien-compatible).
  One acid, three uses — this reaction IS how the cleaner works... it is how
  vault extraction works... and a small tar+acid mix in a lamp is the
  light." The owner's own naming instruction (same sitting): "the utinni
  layer should rename it to our own form of gas. Let's call it Sumpgas" —
  so this def is RUT_-tier by his own explicit word, not the usual
  RM_-tier-content-lands-as-RUT_-for-now stopgap SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1 used
  elsewhere in this kit.

  "Helixien-compatible" — investigated, not guessed. The live def dump
  (vanillaexpanded.helixiengas, package installed and active) was read in
  full for VHGE_Helixien, the mod's own gas ThingDef: it carries
  CompProperties_Forbiddable + CompProperties_CompDestroyOnSpawn and a
  deepCommonality/deepCountPerCell pair matching vanilla's deep-resource
  scatter shape (Gold/Jade's own idiom) — i.e. it is an internal
  scatter/pipenet-feed marker that DESTROYS ITSELF ON SPAWN, not a
  haulable crafting product a recipeMaker could ever output (it would
  vanish the instant the bill finished). So RUT_Sumpgas is its own real,
  haulable, stackable ThingDef — the SAME green-gas substance in flavor and
  name (the ruling's own "leverage that [Helixien] economy"), not a
  disguised VHGE_Helixien. Literal PipeSystem/VHGE_HelixienNet interop
  (piping RUT_Sumpgas through Helixien infrastructure, or vice versa) is
  NOT built this pass — flagged owed, since it would need VHGE's own
  PipeSystem.CompResourceTrader wiring studied live, which this pass had no
  bridge access to verify.

  The reaction itself: a plain vanilla recipeMaker shorthand (same route
  RUT_WeakTarSolvent already uses in this repo) rather than a full
  RecipeDef — costList takes RUT_Bitumen (tar, rendered solid per its own
  header) + RUT_WeakTarSolvent (the acid) together, matching the ruling's
  "reacting it with some acid." Gated behind RUT_GaslightChemistry
  (Defs/ResearchProjectDefs/RUT_Sump_Research.xml, this same item) — a
  plain researchable project for now; wiring it to auto-complete on first
  witnessing a natural flame/geyser (item spec §6, the discovery pilot) is
  explicitly deferred, see that file's own header.

  This is also the byproduct RUT_ScrubTarred now spawns on a successful
  cure (RUT_Tarred_Surgery.xml, this same item, repointed to
  RM_Recipe_RemoveHediffWithByproduct) — "cleaning tar converts it to gas."

  Texture: same placeholder posture as RUT_Bitumen/RUT_ThrummelSeepwax
  (procedurally-drawn, UtinniPatches' own Textures/Things/Item/Resource/
  namespace already claimed per those defs' own headers) — a translucent
  green swirl distinct from both.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_Sumpgas</defName>
    <label>Sumpgas</label>
    <description>Bottled green gas, rendered by working an acid into raw tar until it lets go of its own vapor. The same chemistry the geysers do for free, on demand and by the jug — sharp-smelling, faintly luminous, and the only fuel on the Sump that burns warm instead of foul.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RUT_Sumpgas</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(96, 214, 128)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>30</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>3.2</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.12</Mass>
      <Flammability>1.0</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>4</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <recipeMaker>
      <recipeUsers>
        <li>TableMachining</li>
      </recipeUsers>
      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
      <displayPriority>430</displayPriority>
      <researchPrerequisite>RUT_GaslightChemistry</researchPrerequisite>
      <productCount>3</productCount>
    </recipeMaker>
    <costList>
      <RUT_Bitumen>1</RUT_Bitumen>
      <RUT_WeakTarSolvent>1</RUT_WeakTarSolvent>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
